      "description": "Faculty Careers - The University of Texas at Austin UT Austin Home The University of Texas at Austin Faculty Careers All Positions College of Liberal Arts Religious Studies - 2026-27 Professional Track Faculty Pool Apply now Description The Department of Religious Studies at The University of Texas at Austin seeks to develop a pool of candidates for possible temporary/non-tenure track positions to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses. Positions are not available every semester and are contingent upon student enrollment and the availability of funding. Appointments are normally made on a semester-by-semester basis, though sometimes a yearlong appointment may be made. Positions are renewable annually, contingent upon funding and performance. Qualifications A Ph.D. in a related field and a record of teaching excellence are preferred. Application Instructions Please submit a current curriculum vita and three letters of reference. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University of Texas at Austin, as an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. The University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. College / School / Unit College of Liberal Arts Department Department of Religious Studies Posted Aug 17, 2026 Apply by Aug 15, 2027 Applying UT Austin uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter UT Austin Home Learn more about UT Contact us Phone 512-475-4363 Fax 512-475-7385 Email evpp-aps@utexas.edu 110 Inner Campus Dr. STOP G1000 Austin, TX 78712-1701 Careers Search Why U