    "https://faculty.utexas.edu/career/185016": {
      "title": "Faculty Careers",
      "description": "Faculty Careers - The University of Texas at Austin UT Austin Home The University of Texas at Austin Faculty Careers All Positions College of Liberal Arts Health & Society - 2026-27 Professional Track Faculty Pool Apply now Description The Health and Society program at The University of Texas at Austin seeks to develop a pool of candidates for possible temporary/non-tenure track positions to teach undergraduate courses. Positions are not available every semester and are contingent upon student enrollment and the availability of funding. Appointments are made on a semester-by-semester basis, though sometimes a year-long or years-long appointment can be made. Positions are renewable annually or multi-annually, contingent upon funding, position and performance. Salary is dependent upon position and qualifications. Qualifications A Ph.D. in a social science or humanities discipline that focused on a health-related topic is preferred. Previous college-level teaching experience is required. Application Instructions Interested applicants are invited to submit a curriculum vitae, the names and contact information for three references, and teaching materials (teaching philosophy, teaching evaluations, sample syllabi) to: Shannon Cavanagh, Chair, Department of Sociology; and Stephanie Osbakken and Nina Palmo, Co-Directors, Health and Society Program. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University of Texas at Austin, as an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. The University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. College / School / Unit College of Liberal Arts Department Department of Sociology Posted Aug 16, 2026 Apply by Aug 15, 2027 Applying UT Austin uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter UT Austin Home Learn more about UT Contact us Phone 512-475-4363 Fax 512-475-7385 Email evpp-aps@utexas.edu 110 Inner Campus Dr. STOP G1000 Austin, TX 78712-1701 Careers Search Why UT Life & Work Quicklinks UT Austin Home Site Policies Web Privacy Policy Emergency Information Web Accessibility Policy Adobe Reader"
    },
